---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Recommendation Blocks — Case Study"
  description="Built product recommendations from zero to 80%+ adoption across five regions by designing trust-building three-tier ladder: Manual → Automated → Smart."
>
  <article style="padding: 52px 0;">
    <nav style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <a href="/case-studies" style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">← Back to case studies</a>
    </nav>

    <h1 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-32); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 24px;">Recommendation Blocks</h1>

    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-2); margin-bottom: 32px; max-width: 65ch;">I built the company's product recommendation feature from zero. A three-tier trust ladder let merchants start with high certainty and graduate as confidence grew; 80%+ of merchants who trialled Smart tier adopted it.</p>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">80%+ adoption, Smart tier</span>
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">5 regions · 200ms p99</span>
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">built on the platform ↑</span>
    </div>

    <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 40px;">Node.js · Redis · MongoDB Atlas (multi-region) · ClickHouse · Google Pub/Sub</p>

    <!-- My Role -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 24px;">My Role</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">What I personally owned</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 65ch;">
          <div><strong>Product architecture</strong> — designed three-tier trust model (Manual/Automated/Smart) to reduce merchant risk and enable gradual adoption</div>
          <div><strong>System design</strong> — built multi-region serving, latency SLAs, real-time ranking engine</div>
          <div><strong>Core implementation</strong> — implemented Redis-backed live tier, MongoDB serving layer, ranking algorithm</div>
          <div><strong>Adoption strategy</strong> — worked with sales/success to position tiers, built tier progression measurement and ROI tracking</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">What the product achieved</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 65ch;">
          <div><strong>80%+ Smart-tier adoption</strong> — among merchants who trialled the tier</div>
          <div><strong>Multi-region latency</strong> — 200ms p99 across five regions with real-time ranking</div>
          <div><strong>Merchant trust</strong> — low-friction trust ladder moved from "risky feature" to default-on</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Context -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Context</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">ConvertCart's merchants are SMBs running e-commerce stores. They need product recommendations but are risk-averse: wrong recommendations hurt conversion, cost credibility. If a feature feels unreliable or slow, they turn it off and never come back. Building merchant trust is the core product challenge.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Problem -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Problem</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">ConvertCart doesn't have recommendations. Competitors do. Our merchants need this feature, but want low risk. How do you get a merchant to enable a feature that could hurt their business if it fails? How do you measure success without visibility into merchant behavior? How do you serve real-time ranking across five regions under 200ms?</p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; margin-top: 24px;">
        <div style="padding: 20px; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;">
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">BEFORE</div>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">No recommendations</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Merchant anxiety about feature risk</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink);">No multi-region serving</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 20px; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;">
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">WHY IT MATTERED</div>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Merchants want to increase AOV</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Market expects recommendations</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink);">Feature adoption = retention signal</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Architecture -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Architecture</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">Three-tier ladder: Manual (CSM hand-picks products for each store), Automated (rules-based: "people who bought X also bought Y"), Smart (live behavioral ranking). Each tier uses different computation: Manual is static, Automated is batch-refreshed, Smart is real-time Redis-backed. Merchants graduate as trust builds. Multi-region MongoDB for serving, ClickHouse for analytics.</p>

      <!-- Recommendation Architecture SVG -->
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 480" style="max-width: 65ch; width: 100%; margin-bottom: 24px; display: block;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <defs>
          <style>
            .rec-box { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--rule-2); stroke-width: 1.5; }
            .rec-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; fill: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
            .rec-label-small { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: var(--ink-2); }
            .rec-arrow { stroke: var(--ink-3); stroke-width: 2; fill: none; marker-end: url(#rec-arrowhead); }
          </style>
          <marker id="rec-arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
            <polygon points="0 0, 10 3, 0 6" fill="var(--ink-3)" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Tier progression (left column) -->
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="25" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">TIER PROGRESSION</text>
        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="40" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="65" text-anchor="middle">Manual</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="85" text-anchor="middle">CSM hand-picks</text>
        <line class="rec-arrow" x1="100" y1="100" x2="100" y2="130"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="125" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">trust ↑</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="130" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="155" text-anchor="middle">Automated</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="175" text-anchor="middle">Rules · batch</text>
        <line class="rec-arrow" x1="100" y1="190" x2="100" y2="220"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="215" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">trust ↑</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="20" y="220" width="160" height="80" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label" x="100" y="250" text-anchor="middle">Smart</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="270" text-anchor="middle">(80%+ merchants)</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="100" y="285" text-anchor="middle">Live ranking · Redis</text>

        <!-- Multi-region serving (right column) -->
        <text class="rec-label" x="500" y="25" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">SERVING</text>
        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="40" width="160" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="70" text-anchor="middle">US · EU · APAC</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="100" width="160" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="130" text-anchor="middle">India · Brazil</text>

        <rect class="rec-box" x="420" y="160" width="160" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="185" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;">200ms p99</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="500" y="205" text-anchor="middle">latency SLA</text>

        <!-- Latency tradeoff annotation -->
        <line style="stroke: var(--rule); stroke-width: 1;" x1="40" y1="340" x2="600" y2="340"/>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="320" y="360" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ink-3);">Latency-freshness tradeoff: read replicas lag 5–10s, acceptable for merchant UX</text>
        <text class="rec-label-small" x="320" y="380" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--ink-3);">Redis replication lag reduces on slow replica (fallback to cached tier), prioritizes speed over freshness</text>
      </svg>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Decisions -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Key Decisions</h2>
      <ol style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Three-tier trust model, not one</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Merchants graduate in order, not all-or-nothing. Manual tier proves value, Automated tier proves reliability, Smart tier proves sophistication.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Computation matched to tier, not uniform</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Manual is static, Automated is batch, Smart is live. Allows gradual adoption without building all three systems at once.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Redis-first for latency, durability trade-off</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">In-flight sessions lost on Redis failure is acceptable for recommendations; would not accept this for orders.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">
          <strong>Read replicas trade freshness for speed</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Few seconds of lag serving non-US shoppers beats permanently slow blocks. Asymmetric failure modes.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Execution -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Execution</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Adoption Measurement</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Built tier progression tracking to measure which merchants enabled each tier and how adoption changed over time. The available result: 80%+ of merchants who trialled Smart tier adopted it; timeframe and trial count are not published here.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Conversion Attribution</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Built linkage from orders to specific recommendation blocks. This is what let merchants see ROI. Became the core proof point in sales conversations.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Multi-Region Challenge</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">The serving target was 200ms p99 across five regions: US, EU, APAC, India, and Brazil. Redis replication lag could produce stale rankings, so I used eventual consistency with cached-result fallback when replicas lagged. The page stayed responsive at the cost of slightly older data.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Impact -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Impact</h2>

      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px; padding: 32px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-size: var(--fs-56); font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">80%+ ADOPTION</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0 auto;">Of merchants who trialled, 80%+ graduated to Smart tier</div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">Why It Mattered</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Recommendations became first-party product, not third-party tool.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Conversion attribution proved ROI to merchants.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Feature expanded into multi-channel personalisation.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">Recommendation attribution gave Sales and Customer Success a concrete ROI story for merchant conversations.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">Scale</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">80%+ Smart-tier adoption among trial merchants · five regions · 200ms p99 serving target · attribution used in merchant ROI conversations</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I'd Change Today -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">What I'd Change Today</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">What I'd Preserve</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">The three-tier model was right. Trust-based adoption beats feature-push adoption.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">What I'd Change</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Would invest more in A/B testing infrastructure early (Smart tier had minor bugs that could have been caught faster). Also would have built more merchant-facing dashboards to show performance data in product, not just to sales/success.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <nav class="case-next" aria-label="Related work">
      <a href="/case-studies/data-platform">Related: The data platform →</a>
      <a href="/resume">View resume →</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-next { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-top: 32px; margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
